{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into perception (G1) and motion (G2) to separate uncontrollable sensing from controllable actions. The specification (E1) binds sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative obstacle recovery and steady exploration. E2 prevents repeated recovery actions and ensures full_rotate is used only as a last resort after repeated failures.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and motion into distinct plant automata for clarity and modularity.",
    "Specification automata bind sensor outcomes to actions, enforce safe recovery, and prevent repeated or unsafe behaviors (e.g., repeated rotate or full_rotate)."
  ],
